class DataAdapter:
    'DataAdapter is an abstract class defining an interface for reading/writing\nin/out the contents of a DataTable. It enables access to/from various data\nsources/sinks such as: streams, files, databases and devices. The DataTable\nis independent of the form and format of the data in/out of the source/sink.\nConcrete classes handle the details (e.g. format, sequential access, etc...)\nassociated with a particular data source/sink.\nThe base DataAdapter contains a static registry to serve as a factory for\nconcrete DataAdpaters, given a string identifier of the type of adapter.\nThe adapter knows the source format and data flow (read, write, both).\nString identifiers can be associated with file formats according to known\nfile extensions.'
    ...

    def clone(self, *args: Any, **kwargs: Any) -> Any: ...

    def getDataTable(self, *args: Any, **kwargs: Any) -> Any:
        'Generic interface to retrieve a specific table by name from read result'
        ...

    def read(self, *args: Any, **kwargs: Any) -> Any:
        'Public interface to read data from a dataSourceSpecification, typically a file or folder'
        ...

    def registerDataAdapter(self, *args: Any, **kwargs: Any) -> Any:
        'Register a concrete DataAdapter by its unique string identifier.\n   Registration permits access to the required concrete adapter by\n   identifier lookup. As such, identifiers must be unique, but adapters may\n   be registered with multiple identifiers. For example, a data file may\n   have multiple valid extensions (e.g. ".jpg: and ".jpeg") in which case\n   both extensions would be valid identifiers for the same adapter. If an\n   identifier is already in use an Exception is thrown.\n   All OpenSim data adapters are automatically registered at start of the\n   program.'
        ...

